<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>Attribute Importance</title>
    <style>
        h3 { ${REGULAR_LARGE_FONT_STYLE} }
        body { ${REGULAR_FONT_STYLE} }
        code { ${MONOSPACE_FONT_STYLE} }
        h3 code { font-size: inherit; }
        p { margin-top: 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body style="width: 300px">
    <h3>Attribute Importance</h3>
    <p><strong>Oracle calculation · data-level</strong></p>
    <p><code>DBMS_PREDICTIVE_ANALYTICS.EXPLAIN</code> prepares the data, trains, tests, and scores a temporary model internally, then ranks how useful each input column is for explaining the target. The temporary model is separate from the model shown in this result.</p>
    <p>Oracle returns an explanatory value from 0 (no useful correlation with the target) to 1 (perfect correlation). Each column is calculated independently, so the values do not add up to 1.</p>
    <p>Unlike Attribute Contribution, this is Oracle's direct result about the data and target, not a DBN aggregation of prediction explanations.</p>
</body>
</html>
